WEBVTT

00:00:00.598 --> 00:00:01.550
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.728 --> 00:00:05.310
In this lesson, we do a facial massage, step by step.

00:00:05.965 --> 00:00:09.865
Massage is usually done once the skin is clean, during a facial,

00:00:09.815 --> 00:00:11.790
for about ten to twenty minutes,

00:00:11.975 --> 00:00:13.470
depending on the salon's treatment.

00:00:14.151 --> 00:00:14.927
Step one:

00:00:15.103 --> 00:00:16.127
before you start.

00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:18.127
Review the consultation form.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:23.007
Ask whether the client is allergic to any oils, nuts, or fragrances.

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:24.207
Ask too:

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.207
any recent cosmetic injections, laser, or peels?

00:00:28.537 --> 00:00:32.047
If so, follow the instructions of whoever did the procedure.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:37.327
If there is a cold sore, broken skin, or sunburn, avoid that area.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:41.087
If the client wears contact lenses, ask her to take them out.

00:00:41.255 --> 00:00:43.647
The skin must be clean, with no makeup.

00:00:43.904 --> 00:00:48.207
Then take off your rings and watch, wash your hands with soap, and dry them.

00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:51.007
If your hands are cold, rub them warm first.

00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:52.447
Step two:

00:00:52.723 --> 00:00:53.567
positions.

00:00:54.105 --> 00:00:57.912
The client lies on her back, covered with a towel and a blanket,

00:00:57.862 --> 00:01:00.847
leaving only the face, neck and shoulders exposed.

00:01:01.282 --> 00:01:04.527
Ask whether she is warm enough, and whether the pillow is comfortable.

00:01:04.951 --> 00:01:06.927
You sit on a stool at the head of the bed.

00:01:07.435 --> 00:01:10.577
Adjust it so your back is straight, your shoulders relaxed,

00:01:10.527 --> 00:01:11.887
and your wrists straight.

00:01:12.395 --> 00:01:13.887
And tell the client beforehand:

00:01:14.168 --> 00:01:17.567
if the pressure is too firm, or too light, just let me know.

00:01:18.187 --> 00:01:19.498
Today's order is:

00:01:19.607 --> 00:01:25.384
shoulders and neck, jaw and cheeks, around the mouth, forehead, around the eyes,

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.458
pressure holds,

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:27.498
and then the finish.

00:01:27.985 --> 00:01:32.302
Work from the bottom up, from the least sensitive areas to the most sensitive,

00:01:32.252 --> 00:01:33.178
around the eyes.

00:01:33.522 --> 00:01:37.360
Keep the same order every time, so your hands get used to it,

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:40.218
your rhythm stays even, and no area is missed.

00:01:40.805 --> 00:01:41.673
Step three:

00:01:42.002 --> 00:01:42.633
the oil.

00:01:43.096 --> 00:01:47.113
Pump a small amount into your palm, and rub your hands together to warm it.

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:48.792
Start with just a little.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.913
If your hands drag on the skin, add a little more.

00:01:52.287 --> 00:01:57.193
Too much, and the face gets greasy, and your hands slip, and are hard to control.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:58.711
Step four:

00:01:58.957 --> 00:01:59.911
the first touch.

00:02:00.578 --> 00:02:03.641
Place both hands on the client's shoulders, gently,

00:02:03.591 --> 00:02:05.591
and hold still for a few breaths.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.991
Then press the shoulders down lightly.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.071
This touch tells the client:

00:02:10.309 --> 00:02:12.471
we are starting now, you can relax.

00:02:13.118 --> 00:02:14.078
Step five:

00:02:14.262 --> 00:02:15.598
neck and shoulders.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.289
Stroke lightly with your palms down the sides of the neck, toward the collarbone,

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.678
then out to the shoulders.

00:02:22.185 --> 00:02:24.146
Do not touch the middle of the throat,

00:02:24.096 --> 00:02:26.558
and don't press deep into the sides of the neck.

00:02:26.902 --> 00:02:29.758
Repeat a few times, slowly and evenly.

00:02:30.346 --> 00:02:31.219
Step six:

00:02:31.408 --> 00:02:32.579
jaw and cheeks.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:37.459
Stroke from the center of the chin, along the jawline, up to the front of the ear.

00:02:37.871 --> 00:02:42.259
Then stroke from beside the nose, under the cheekbones, up to the temples.

00:02:42.678 --> 00:02:44.979
Both hands mirror each other, evenly.

00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:49.299
The direction is always upward and outward, never dragging the skin down.

00:02:49.946 --> 00:02:50.817
Step seven:

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:51.857
circles.

00:02:52.443 --> 00:02:57.169
The tips of your middle and ring fingers draw small, light circles on the cheeks,

00:02:57.119 --> 00:02:58.497
then along the jawline.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.457
Each circle moves up a little, working gradually from the chin to the temples.

00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:05.137
Light, even pressure.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.453
Next, around the mouth.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.798
Place your middle fingertips at the center of the chin,

00:03:10.748 --> 00:03:13.613
and stroke around the lips up to the sides of the nose,

00:03:13.721 --> 00:03:14.733
very lightly.

00:03:15.322 --> 00:03:19.453
Then stroke from the corners of the mouth out to the sides, toward the ears.

00:03:20.029 --> 00:03:23.453
Don't pull the corners of the mouth, and don't get oil on the lips.

00:03:23.694 --> 00:03:27.672
Do each movement about three to six times before you move to the next area,

00:03:27.622 --> 00:03:29.453
so the client has time to feel it,

00:03:29.641 --> 00:03:30.413
and relax.

00:03:31.059 --> 00:03:31.945
Step eight:

00:03:32.163 --> 00:03:32.905
the forehead.

00:03:33.508 --> 00:03:38.347
Place your palms on the forehead, and stroke from the brows up to the hairline,

00:03:38.297 --> 00:03:40.105
one hand following the other,

00:03:40.134 --> 00:03:40.905
slowly.

00:03:41.257 --> 00:03:45.145
Then stroke across, from the center of the forehead out to the temples.

00:03:45.574 --> 00:03:49.225
The forehead is where many people hold tension when they are tired or worried.

00:03:49.615 --> 00:03:53.465
Here, go a little slower, and let the client breathe evenly.

00:03:54.094 --> 00:03:54.991
Step nine:

00:03:55.171 --> 00:03:56.191
around the eyes.

00:03:56.504 --> 00:03:59.311
Use only your ring finger, with the lightest pressure.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:02.138
Glide along the brows out to the temples,

00:04:02.088 --> 00:04:05.231
then circle very lightly along the bone under the eye,

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.671
toward the bridge of the nose.

00:04:07.106 --> 00:04:08.751
Do not press on the eyelids.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.431
If the client wears contact lenses, they have already been taken out.

00:04:12.781 --> 00:04:15.231
And take care not to let oil run into the eyes.

00:04:15.884 --> 00:04:16.677
Step ten:

00:04:17.016 --> 00:04:18.037
pressure holds.

00:04:18.786 --> 00:04:23.114
Press slowly with your fingertips between the brows, then under the cheekbones,

00:04:23.064 --> 00:04:24.197
then at the temples.

00:04:24.621 --> 00:04:27.317
Hold for a few seconds, then release slowly.

00:04:27.906 --> 00:04:29.957
Ask the client whether the pressure is right.

00:04:30.325 --> 00:04:34.357
For red or sensitive skin, press very lightly, or skip it.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:39.304
If you want to tap lightly, the fingertips touch the cheeks quickly and lightly,

00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:40.277
like falling rain.

00:04:40.457 --> 00:04:42.277
No tapping on sensitive skin.

00:04:42.929 --> 00:04:43.800
Step eleven:

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:44.840
the finish.

00:04:45.305 --> 00:04:50.332
Stroke long over the whole face, from the chin to the cheeks, to the forehead,

00:04:50.282 --> 00:04:51.800
and out to the temples,

00:04:51.829 --> 00:04:53.720
a few times, getting slower.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:57.291
Finally, a light pressure hold on both temples,

00:04:57.241 --> 00:04:59.880
then lift your hands away very slowly.

00:05:00.211 --> 00:05:05.240
If a mask comes next, remove the excess oil with warm, damp sponges.

00:05:05.865 --> 00:05:09.327
Throughout the massage, there are a few very common mistakes.

00:05:09.755 --> 00:05:12.687
Lifting both hands off and putting them back suddenly:

00:05:12.813 --> 00:05:13.966
the client is startled.

00:05:14.466 --> 00:05:16.047
Always keep a hand on the client.

00:05:16.556 --> 00:05:18.047
Nails touching the skin:

00:05:18.388 --> 00:05:19.567
nails must be short;

00:05:19.669 --> 00:05:21.567
use only the pads of your fingertips.

00:05:22.008 --> 00:05:23.327
Talking all the time:

00:05:23.437 --> 00:05:24.767
the client can't relax.

00:05:25.159 --> 00:05:27.807
Ask about the pressure, then let the client rest.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:29.647
And forgetting to watch the skin:

00:05:29.816 --> 00:05:33.807
wherever it reddens quickly, lighten your touch, or skip that area.

00:05:34.307 --> 00:05:38.790
If the skin turns red, stings or itches, stop, wipe gently,

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:42.847
and apply a cool compress, as in the incidents lesson.

00:05:43.479 --> 00:05:44.363
Step twelve:

00:05:44.613 --> 00:05:45.643
after the massage.

00:05:46.038 --> 00:05:49.163
Ask the client how she feels, and whether the pressure was right.

00:05:49.494 --> 00:05:50.043
Tell her:

00:05:50.321 --> 00:05:55.083
if redness, stinging or itching lasts, let the salon know right away.

00:05:55.507 --> 00:05:58.923
Write it in the internal notes on the client record in VaraaAi:

00:05:59.194 --> 00:06:03.003
the oil used, the pressure she likes, and the areas to avoid.

00:06:03.282 --> 00:06:05.323
Next time, whoever does it will know.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:06.363
Then clean up:

00:06:06.591 --> 00:06:11.007
towels and headbands into a laundry basket with a lid, wipe down the bed,

00:06:10.957 --> 00:06:12.203
and wash your hands.

00:06:12.536 --> 00:06:15.403
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
